cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite the paper below. The manuscript is under
  review and the target venue is not yet confirmed; the citation metadata will
  be updated when the venue is assigned.
title: "KAP-Flow: Bridging Pilot Observations and Propagation Knowledge for MIMO Channel Estimation"
abstract: >-
  Pilot-limited MIMO channel estimation must infer components beyond the
  pilot-observable subspace. KAP-Flow is a channel-knowledge-map (CKM)
  conditioned FlowADMM receiver for mobile users: location-queried propagation
  statistics, user state and time-frequency coordinates condition a shared
  straight-flow prior (knowledge-and-state conditioning, KSC), and a
  noise-aware complex-domain pilot update, conditional prior refinement and
  dual feedback combine this prior with the current measurements
  (pilot-prior consensus, PPC). Across three simulated sites and nine SNRs,
  joint conditioning improves aggregate NMSE by 2.27 dB, and with the same
  conditional prior KAP-Flow outperforms PnP-Flow by 4.25 dB.
